      "cml:integrityHash": "b7d9037a20f00b21d641020db363e38285f91806ce5a2ff9cf410d45508fe6d9",
      "skos:note": "Service rendered in connection with treatment under relevant DVA law must be reported.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/health-legislation-amendment-data-matching-and-other-matters-act-2019#sch-2-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Subsection 81(1) (after paragraph (b) of the definition of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "service)\nInsert:\n\n; or (c) a service that:\n\n(i) has been rendered in connection with the provision of\ntreatment under a relevant DVA law; and\n\n(ii) is of a kind that, if the service had not been rendered in\nconnection with the provision of treatment under the\nrelevant DVA law, medicare benefit or dental benefit\nwould have been payable in respect of the service."
